brane-deployment prohject structure
==================================
brane-k8s-deployment/ 
├── inventories/ 
│   └── production/
│       └── hosts.ini            # Defines VM host IPs and deployment variables 
├── roles/ 
│   ├── k3s_setup/               # Role to provision the multi-node K3s cluster 
│   │   └── tasks/ 
│   │       └── main.yml 
│   ├── brane_secrets/           # Role to handle certificate generation & K8s secrets 
│   │   └── tasks/ 
│   │       └── main.yml 
│   └── brane_helm/              # Role to manage the Helm chart lifecycle 
│       └── tasks/ │           └── main.yml 
├── group_vars/ 
│   └── all.yml                  # Global configurations (versions, chart paths) 
├── brane-chart/                 # The complete Helm Chart directory tree 
│   ├── Chart.yaml 
│   ├── values.yaml 
│   └── templates/ 
│       ├── central-hub.yaml 
│       └── worker-nodes.yaml 
└── deploy.yml                   # The master playbook driving the entire execution

Verification and Monitoring
============================

Once executed, management commands shift away from raw host configuration tasks. You can manage and inspect your entire cluster natively using standard Kubernetes tools:

Bash

# Check the deployment status of your containers across all VMs
kubectl get pods -o wide

# Check the automatically provisioned persistent data volumes
kubectl get pvc

# Stream runtime execution logs from worker node 1
kubectl logs -l app=brane-worker,instance=client-node-1 --follow

How to Run the Deployment
==========================

Simply point the main deployment playbook to your target inventory directory structure from the terminal root path:

ansible-playbook -i inventories/production/hosts.ini deploy.yml

